[1]//! `hof_game` 鈥?the scaffolded Bevy 0.19.1 game.
[2]//!
[3]//! This file is the **same binary in both modes** (PRD 搂3-C1): with
[4]//! `HOF_GAME_HEADLESS` set it runs with no window and no render world, and
[5]//! without it, it opens one real window.  Every round of the pipeline runs it
[6]//! headless, because SPIKE-2 measured windowed mode at 4.0 FPS on this machine,
[7]//! which is far too slow to observe a jump arc.
[8]//!
[9]//! Three facts from the spike reports are load-bearing here and must not be
[10]//! "tidied away":
[11]//!
[12]//! 1. **`ScheduleRunnerPlugin` is mandatory in headless mode.**  Without it the
[13]//!    app runs one frame and exits with code 0, and the BRP endpoint is never
[14]//!    bound (SPIKE-2 C7).
[15]//! 2. **`WgpuSettings { backends: None }` means "no render world at all"**, not
[16]//!    "an empty one": Bevy never adds `ExtractPlugin`, so port 15703 does not
[17]//!    exist.  The adapter depends on 15702 only.
[18]//! 3. **The observation surface is declared, not inferred.**  `RemotePlugin` +
[19]//!    `RemoteHttpPlugin` open 15702 on loopback with no authentication, which is
[20]//!    why this build exists for development and CI only.
[21]
[22]use std::time::Duration;
[23]
